Date: Wed, 2 Nov 1994 13:35:59 +0100 (MET)
Subject: [#94-11-27] Other uses of Zen Enlightenment

Reilly Jones wrote:
>These insights are what I was referring to as fruits of long-jump searches in
>knowledge space.  It doesn't happen very often, but there have been new vistas
>opened up for human experiences to travel to, by mystics throughout history.
 
Another area where mysticism can possibly be very useful is in uploading
and coping with drastic changes in physical/mental medium. I have noted
that most current discussions about uploading focus mainly on the
technical aspects but not on the psychological problems. In order to
achieve successful uploading we have to find methods to deal with the
existential problems many uploaders may feel, the emotional shock of no
longer being human and many other problems. 

One use of Zen could be to make uploaders less fixated on their exact
ego-construct, and instead try to deal with the drastic changes around
(and in) them in a calm, logical way without worrying too much about
exactly who or what they currently are (at least in an uncontrollable
fashion). It might also be useful latter on, to help an uploaded person
gradually overcome its dependency on existing as just a single
"consciousness-thread" and instead run in parallel or distributed mode (it
would be very hard for a person used to existing as a single, undivided
being to run in parallel with itself). 

 
